      },
      "blurb": "Unlikely but effective volus mercenary operative",
      "publicNotes": "<p>Volus commandos are rare enough that most opponents underestimate them exactly once. The pressure suit that looks like a liability is rated for vacuum and chemical environments; the figure waddling toward you has survived conditions that would kill an unprotected turian. Their technical proficiency means their weapons function reliably where others struggle, and their commercial expertise means resupply arrives in places where other mercenaries are rationing rounds.</p><p><strong>Pressure Suit:</strong> +2 circ. bonus to Fortitude saves vs. disease, poison, and environmental hazards.</p><p><strong>Tech Grenade (2 actions):</strong> Hurls an electromagnetic grenade at a point within 30 ft. All creatures in a 10-ft burst must succeed at a DC 21 Reflex save or take 3d6 electricity damage and become flat-footed until the end of their next turn (half damage on a success, no flat-footed).</p><p><strong>Kinetic Barrier:</strong> 50 Shield HP. Recharges 10 HP per turn.</p>",
